<h2>Questions from Duluth property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you travel to North Shore cabins?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We inspect properties in Duluth and along the North Shore and elsewhere in the Arrowhead. Remote sites may take a little more scheduling.</p></div></details><details><summary>My Duluth basement flooded in a storm. Is that an appraisal issue?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It depends on the source. Sewer backup under an endorsement can often go to appraisal once accepted. Surface water is usually a flood insurance matter with its own process.</p></div></details></div>
